o jump  like that and then that'll make sure  that's not on a weak link when you're  using your jumping technique another way  to train the muscles in your foot not  only for jump height but also for  balance is to use something like this  these are Vibram FiveFingers  be very careful because they can be hard  on your knees if you're not used to them  you need to work your way up start on  soft surfaces but these are basically  shoes that have got flexible toes and  what that allows you to do is to run to  climb to jump and to use the muscles in  your feet as you do which of course will  improve your billets to use them like  the Terra muhammara tribe who can run  huge distances without tiring out and  who never seem to fall over because  they've got so much strength and  stability in their ankles and in their  feet I've talked a little bit about  stretching in order to improve your  muscle spindle sensitivity and to allow  yourself to land more quietly but it  also has other benefits including  boosting your jump height that might  sound strange but that's because when a  muscle is tight and it's not at all  flexible it actually constantly exerts  force and resistance during your  movements so we have a muscle in the  front of our leg  in our Shin called the tibialis anterior  and this pulls our foot up all the time  so if that's tense if you haven't  stretched and loosened that up it's  constantly pulling your foot up so when  you try and jump and you're trying to  launch off the ground and put your foot  down it's fighting you so you need to  stretch and flex that muscle there and  then this will allow you to jump more  easily because you're removing that  resistance so just pulling your leg up  behind you and making sure to feel the  bend on your foot as well as your leg  will help you to train that and then you  should find not only can you jump higher  you can also even run faster running  fast is another of Black Panthers  abilities of course and all the training  we've discussed so far improving your  flexibility your foot muscles your  explosiveness that'll help you to run  faster at the same time you can also  find the link in the description down  below to another of my videos talking  about how to run fast like sonic and  you'll find many more tips on speed  drills etc that you can use there  finally the last thing you might want to  train in order to be more like Black  Panther is our senses because Black  Panther has super acute senses a bit  like wolverine or daredevil and that's  something else that allows them to fight  with amazing reflexes and to not get  snuck up on but even for a panther  cannot hear his victim  so how can we improve our senses well  once again this is something I've  already covered a little video I'm  training like daredevil I'll link to  that in the description down below but  just to go over the basics you want to  focus on using your senses in a cross  modal fashion so not focusing just on  your site or on your hearing but I'm  focusing on sound localization so that  means listening for things and then  working out where they came from in  space so a good exercise is to support  your mind for a moment listen to sounds  around you then try and guess where they  are and then find them and that's the  kind of training that they actually  teach to time-waster sound engineering  students they surrounded in a circle  they wear blindfold and have to identify  where sounds are coming from because  really that's what would be useful in a  fight isn't it knowing where someone  sneaking up on you or where an attack is  coming from so focus on not only  listening for sounds but working out  where they're coming from and using your  senses together if you're going to  practice walking through the house with  blindfold on trying not to break  anything including your own limbs then  something you can do is to focus not  only on your tactile senses but also on  sound also on temperature it's actually  we have many more than five senses and  by using them together you can get much  more information so if you're walking  through your house you might try and  feel the breeze coming from from a  window or you might try and feel a  change in the texture on the ground or a  creaky floorboard all these things can  give you more information about where  you are and it's using them together  like this that allow you to improve your  senses but a lot of its just mindfulness  it's focusing on those senses not just  ignoring them because there's so much  information that we ignore all the time  and when you become more mindful as  we've seen with the proprioceptive by  focusing on your limb length and things  like that you can increase your  awareness of that thing and thicken the  brain matter that helps you to be more  sensitive to that information we have  brain plasticity showing that you can  form more neurons corresponding to  different activities and abilities but  you also have visual plasticity meaning  that you can increase the number of  photoreceptors in your eye potentially  the studies that look at this are mainly  focusing on rehabilitation rather than  heightening your senses but in theory  it's possible to grow new receptors to  increase your visual acuity and  where you might do this is by focusing  more on your peripheral vision which we  don't pay much attention to we tend to  have a very narrow focused view and this  could actually birth new receptors to  increase our cutie in the periphery of  our vision and once again that's the  kind of sense that would be useful to a  black panther because it would allow you  to again see things creeping up and you  know where they're coming from and in  the sound localization and then you are  like you're like a cat I talked in a  previous video on how to use a technique  called splatter vision or wide-angle  vision or owl eyes in order to engage  your peripheral vision and a way to  practice this is to put your arms out by  your sides  to focus on your fingers like so and  then to keep your vision spread out like  that you lose a lot of the detail that  you get from focused vision but at the  same time you're taking in more  information and you're more aware of  your surroundings go and check out that  video if you want more information on  that but this researchers desk that  practicing this could actually increase  the number of photoreceptors in your  peripheral vision and thereby greatly  enhance your ability to see things  coming from either side today I hope  your fans video useful interesting guys  if you did then please leave a like  please share it around please comment  down below let me know what you think if  I missed anything if you can think of  any cool techniques that might be useful  to train more like Black Panther I've  got many more videos like this on the  way so stay tuned if you want more on  bodybuilding fitness martial arts  productivity transhumanism technology  nootropics if that all sounds good then  thanks a ton for watching I really mean  that  and bye for now
 

